Phase A — Schemas & Types

 Create packages/schemas with Protobuf/FlatBuffers for TopOfBook, MarketMeta, OrderBundle, Execution.

 Generate TS and Rust bindings (Buf or flatc).

 Add packages/utils/decimal.ts with exact decimal ops & rounding helpers (and Rust equivalent).

Phase B — Gateway (Node/TS)

 Implement socket.ts:

Connect with transports: ['websocket'], version pin.

Subscribe to all required markets (build list from markets metadata).

Normalize messages → TopOfBook; compute K-level micro-depth.

Push to engine over UDS (binary frames).

 Implement rest.ts:

placeOrder({market, side, qty, tif, price?})

Idempotent clientOrderId (ULID ≤ 36 chars).

Retry/backoff with per-route rate limiter.

 Implement private.ts:

Auth handshake.

Listen for order & balance events; persist to ClickHouse.

 Implement server.ts:

/bundles endpoint accepting OrderBundle for manual tests.

Health endpoints /healthz, /readyz.

 Export Prometheus metrics via /metrics.

Phase C — Engine (Rust)

 Build market graph:

Load MarketMeta map; enumerate triangles, build trianglesByMarket index.

 Tick pipeline:

MPSC (bounded) channel from UDS → worker threads → compute.

Compute edge & sizing with constraints, K-level liquidity guard.

Cooldown & de-dup logic.

 Emit OrderBundle to gateway over UDS.

 Expose metrics with prometheus crate.

 Config via config.toml + env overrides.

Phase D — Storage & Ops

 ClickHouse client in gateway; buffered insert (every 200ms or 5k rows).

 Grafana dashboards (JSON) + Prometheus alerts (YAML).

 Dockerfiles: small Alpine base, non-root user.

 Terraform: VPC + EC2 in ap-south-1, SG egress only; IAM role for secrets.

Phase E — Testing

 Unit tests for math/precision (TS + Rust).

 Integration test harness: fake depth generator → expect bundles.

 Backtester: load ticks CSV → policy → P&L report.